---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Partner with The V Spot Network" description="Sponsor The V Spot Network, partner on Camp Tralee or NRF dinners, and build a useful 2027 programme with Vinny O'Brien." type="WebPage">
  <main class="wrap commercial">
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="kicker">The commercial desk · Tralee, Ireland · Across the Atlantic</p>
      <h1>Partner with<br /><span>The V Spot</span></h1>
      <p class="standfirst">Good stories travel. Good partnerships give them somewhere to go.</p>
      <p>The V Spot Network brings together commerce operators, founders, technology teams and the people who have to make the platforms work on Monday morning. We make video, podcasts, essays, live conversations and the occasional joke at the expense of the industry we love.</p>
      <p>For 2027, we’re building partner programmes around useful ideas, credible audiences and formats people actually want to watch or attend. Rate cards and tailored plans are available.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/book/">Talk partnership with Vinny</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="#opportunities">See the opportunities</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section id="opportunities">
      <p class="grid-label">The green room</p>
      <h2>Choose your entrance</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="number">01 / ON AIR</span>
          <h3>Back a show</h3>
          <p>Work with Nearly News, The Struggle Bus or The Ostrich Report through a season, a focused campaign or a format built around your audience.</p>
          <p class="aside">Video, editorial, operator conversations and distribution. Editorial control stays with The V Spot; sponsor involvement is agreed up front.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="mailto:vinny@vinnyandco.com?subject=V%20Spot%20partnership%20rate%20card">Ask for the current rate card →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="number">02 / ON LOCATION</span>
          <h3>Join Camp Tralee</h3>
          <p>A proposed gathering for commerce operators in County Kerry: thoughtful conversations, good company and a room with fewer stage lights than opinions.</p>
          <p class="aside">Founding partner conversations are open. Date, venue and final partner benefits are still being confirmed.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/backstage/camp-tralee/">Open the Camp Tralee pass →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="number">03 / NEW YORK</span>
          <h3>Host an NRF dinner</h3>
          <p>A small, brand-led dinner alongside NRF 2027, designed to make room for proper conversation away from the show floor.</p>
          <p class="aside">Partner interest is being gathered. Date and venue remain subject to confirmation.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/backstage/nrf-dinner/">Open the NRF dinner pass →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="number">04 / THE BIGGER PICTURE</span>
          <h3>Build a 2027 programme</h3>
          <p>Connect the show, the editorial work and live experiences into a partnership with a point of view—and a sensible reason to keep going.</p>
          <p class="aside">We’ll shape the mix around your audience, goals and calendar, then agree the work and measures before we start.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/backstage/2027-partnerships/">Open the 2027 partner pass →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="number">05 / LIVE</span>
          <h3>Book Vinny to speak or host</h3>
          <p>Keynotes, panels and event hosting on commerce, technology, AI and the human beings asked to live with both.</p>
          <p class="aside">Talks shaped from original essays and two decades of operator-side experience.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/speaking/">See speaking topics →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-red">
          <span class="number">DECEMBER / SHORT RUN</span>
          <h3>Get in before the year ends</h3>
          <p>A small number of quick-turn partner slots are available across The V Spot’s year-end programming. Brief, timing and fit first; logo confetti later.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/backstage/2027-partnerships/">Ask about a December slot →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing">
      <p class="kicker">A note from the desk</p>
      <h2>Make it useful. Make it memorable. Let it sound like us.</h2>
      <p>We’ll agree the audience, the work, the approvals and the delivery dates before anything goes on air. No mystery inventory. No surprise invoices. No claiming the joke was focus-grouped.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/book/">Start a conversation</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="mailto:vinny@vinnyandco.com?subject=Partner%20with%20The%20V%20Spot">Email the commercial desk</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
<style>
.commercial { padding-top: 54px; padding-bottom: 72px; }
.hero { max-width: 860px; padding: 34px 0 58px; }
.kicker,.number { font: 700 .75rem/1.5 var(--mono); color: var(--tan); letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.hero h1 { font: 4.5rem/1.02 var(--display); letter-spacing: .02em; margin: 16px 0 18px; color: var(--paper); }
.hero h1 span { color: #ff6b6d; text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(232,39,42,.4); }
.standfirst { font-size: 1.45rem; color: var(--tan); max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.hero > p:not(.kicker):not(.standfirst) { color: #d0d1da; max-width: 740px; margin: 12px 0; }
.actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 28px; }
.button { display: inline-block; padding: 12px 18px; text-decoration: none; font: 700 .76rem/1.3 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid var(--tan); }
.button.primary { background: var(--red); border-color: var(--red); color: white; }
.button.secondary { color: var(--paper); }
.button:hover,.button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--tan); outline-offset: 3px; }
h2 { font: 2.2rem/1.15 var(--display); color: var(--paper); margin: 0 0 24px; }
.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(270px,1fr)); gap: 16px; }
.card { background: #12172d; border: 1px solid #343a58; padding: 24px; min-height: 260px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
.card h3 { font: 1.45rem/1.2 var(--display); margin: 12px 0; }
.card p { color: #d0d1da; }
.card .aside { color: var(--grey); font-size: .9rem; margin-top: 12px; }
.card .text-link { color: #ff8a8c; margin-top: auto; padding-top: 20px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
.card .text-link:hover,.card .text-link:focus-visible { text-decoration: underline; }
.card-red { border-color: var(--red); background: linear-gradient(145deg,#281725,#12172d 70%); }
.closing { margin-top: 72px; padding: 32px; border-top: 2px solid var(--red); background: #10152b; }
.closing h2 { max-width: 700px; margin-top: 12px; }
.closing > p:not(.kicker) { max-width: 700px; color: #d0d1da; }
@media(max-width:600px) { .hero h1 { font-size: 3rem; } .closing { padding: 24px; } }
</style>
